 "estimator_note": "Tier 'context re-map' (open squares) fits source-context -> target-context on a POOLED source that has no per-row counterpart for a cell's rows (the cell is a SUBSET of the pool), so it optimizes a different composite objective than the pair-ladder's rung-7 paired target->source context ridge and is NOT comparable to rung 7. Empirically it collapses: context-arm median fraction of own ceiling reads pooled_direct +0.872, rotation_bias +0.921, ctx_remap +0.066, ans_remap +1.040 (scripts/issue2054_pooled_tier_ladder.py docstring)."
